WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:01.650
OK.

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:06.320
Let's now dig further into the idea of what
government should and shouldn't be involved

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:10.650
in, which is a really major part of the conversation
about police departments.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:15.769
We've already talked about calls to abolish
or defund the police in light of the protests

00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:17.710
and the killing of George Floyd.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:22.840
There's a bigger question implicit in that
discussion, which is what should governments

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.640
be involved in and what shouldn't governments
be involved in?

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.020
And this is a question that really tracks
political views, because on one side, you

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:35.130
have extreme small government conservatives
and libertarians.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.000
They will sometimes go as far as to say roads
should be privatized.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.540
You can pay the owner to use whichever road
you want or look for a different road.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:48.890
Another example would be the privatization
of law enforcement, where if you want to be

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:53.850
able to call the police, you pay some kind
of a membership fee to the law enforcement

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:58.810
company that you prefer Google cops or Amazon
police or whatever.

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:03.580
These are extreme examples, but there are
some small government libertarians that believe

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:04.760
this stuff.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:09.740
On the extreme other hand, you have truly
communist governments where the government

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:13.500
would potentially own all of the industry
and be the sole employer.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.540
They manufacture the vehicles, the government
employs the doctors, owns the hospitals, owns

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.430
every restaurant, decides what food rations
people get and what farmers need to do with

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.500
the crops that they grow.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.890
These are two extremes.

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:32.660
We have no examples of success in the modern
world for either of the two extremes, because

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:36.070
like with most things, the devil is in the
details.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:39.210
This is gray area, so let's dig into it.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:44.200
My starting point as a social Democrat is
that there are many things government should

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:49.510
be doing instead of private industry, but
we should be able to articulate a compelling

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:53.760
reason for why the government should be involved
instead of private industry.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:58.810
So in other words, government should not be
the only provider of a good or service unless

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:05.979
there is a specific case about why they should
be one of the most important things that governments

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:11.879
should be doing in industries where they are
not participating is setting the ground rules,

00:02:11.879 --> 00:02:13.769
which I call regulation.

00:02:13.769 --> 00:02:19.349
I don't need government providing, for example,
car insurance, but I do want government saying

00:02:19.349 --> 00:02:24.999
to private businesses, if you want to be in
the market of offering car insurance.

00:02:24.999 --> 00:02:27.420
Here are the rules you have to abide by.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:32.819
Similarly, I don't want the government running
airlines and making the airplanes, but I do

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:37.739
want government heavily involved in saying
if you're going to build airplanes, here are

00:02:37.739 --> 00:02:39.139
the ground rules.

00:02:39.139 --> 00:02:44.069
If you are going to sell tickets to fly, people
around here are the ground rules you need

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:45.069
to adhere to.

00:02:45.069 --> 00:02:47.540
Now, most examples are pretty easy to get
agreement on.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:52.260
For example, very few people believe the government
should be the sole manufacture.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:56.450
Of mobile phones, and we've got plenty of
companies, Samsung, Apple and others that

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:00.700
are innovating in that space and making mobile
phones, and that's fine.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:05.409
But we'll get back to mobile phones because
there are complexities that come in when you

00:03:05.409 --> 00:03:08.780
introduce externality is which justify the
role of government.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:13.799
Now, on the other hand, most people do believe
that governments should be responsible for

00:03:13.799 --> 00:03:19.980
police departments and law enforcement, missile
defense, defending the country from foreign

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:23.790
attackers, stopping terrorism, et cetera.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:28.379
And as I mentioned in the other segment, you
might think that it's a good idea to leave

00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:32.390
something like human trafficking to nonprofits
and community groups.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:38.529
But this is stuff with such a massive legal
infrastructure and it's so big and wide ranging.

00:03:38.529 --> 00:03:44.159
I do want a properly functioning government
law enforcement apparatus to be dealing with

00:03:44.159 --> 00:03:46.730
something like human trafficking correctly.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:50.530
So the small government versus big government
ideas are very often theoretical.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.019
They're about principles.

00:03:52.019 --> 00:03:57.689
But you've got to do way more work to really
figure out how our economy should be organized.

00:03:57.689 --> 00:04:01.919
Health care is something I want government
more involved in health care.

00:04:01.919 --> 00:04:06.879
There are examples from all over the world
of government being involved in health care

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.049
and the health care being better.

00:04:09.049 --> 00:04:10.890
Health care is an exception.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:15.629
As I mentioned, we need a compelling reason
to say this should be pulled out of for profit

00:04:15.629 --> 00:04:16.979
markets.

00:04:16.979 --> 00:04:22.920
When we're talking about people's health,
I don't believe at a moral level that that

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:29.430
should be something subject to the whims of
companies looking to make profits.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:35.669
So as a social Democrat, I would say health
care meets the requirement to be pulled out

00:04:35.669 --> 00:04:38.110
of for profit market based.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.419
And then you've got gray area.

00:04:39.419 --> 00:04:43.960
So, like, I don't need the government running
all the hospitals or employing all the doctors

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.250
necessarily.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:49.490
But maybe I just want them being the insurance
company, negotiating prices, establishing

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:50.490
ground rules, OK?

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.500
That that's something that that I would want.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.159
Let me give you another gray area.

00:04:55.159 --> 00:04:57.889
I want the government doing lots of infrastructure
spending.

00:04:57.889 --> 00:05:01.250
I want them improving our airports and our
roads and our bridges.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:06.159
I don't need the government running the construction
companies or being the construction company

00:05:06.159 --> 00:05:09.840
and buying the bulldozers and the skids steers
and doing it all themselves.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:16.159
I'm fine with government hiring private industry
to do the actual infrastructure work.

00:05:16.159 --> 00:05:21.729
The problem is when the process of hiring
private industry becomes a crony capitalist

00:05:21.729 --> 00:05:25.419
snow job where the jobs are given to the president's
friends.

00:05:25.419 --> 00:05:27.379
So I'm a social Democrat.

00:05:27.379 --> 00:05:34.819
I do think that markets, when they actually
are well regulated and function fairly direct

00:05:34.819 --> 00:05:40.759
resources where they are most useful from
a utility point of view.

00:05:40.759 --> 00:05:48.710
And sometimes we have to say this area of
society should not be subjected to the market

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:52.830
calculation of where the most utility is derived.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.819
Health being one of those examples.

00:05:54.819 --> 00:06:00.110
I don't believe for a second this B.S. that
we hear about industries have incentives to

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:01.789
regulate themselves.

00:06:01.789 --> 00:06:05.689
Government doesn't need to regulate because
if the business does something bad, the PR

00:06:05.689 --> 00:06:06.689
will be terrible.

00:06:06.689 --> 00:06:09.830
News reports about them will make them lose
money.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.479
Just doesn't work, doesn't work.

00:06:11.479 --> 00:06:15.909
Consider a company that makes cars and they
pollute and harm some town that's downwind

00:06:15.909 --> 00:06:20.349
and people in that town get way more lung
cancer over the 20 years after the cars have

00:06:20.349 --> 00:06:21.349
been manufactured.

00:06:21.349 --> 00:06:22.349
That's an externality.

00:06:22.349 --> 00:06:27.560
Now, you could say, well, the bad PR of people
hearing about that is going to make fewer

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:30.000
people buy that company's cars.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.419
And so the company has an incentive not to
pollute in order to keep selling more cars

00:06:34.419 --> 00:06:36.950
and avoid the bad PR just doesn't happen.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:43.580
These externalities are only often loosely
assignable to a specific action by a company.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:48.819
Oftentimes, even if the company gets sued,
it is cheaper to pollute and kill a bunch

00:06:48.819 --> 00:06:50.069
of people and everyone.

00:06:50.069 --> 00:06:54.259
So in a while you just pay some civil lawsuit.

00:06:54.259 --> 00:07:00.639
So the point here is the externalities are
not properly dealt with by markets and that

00:07:00.639 --> 00:07:02.780
is the role of government regulation.

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:09.460
So the takeaway is I want most areas of life
operating in well regulated markets with the

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:14.860
profits properly taxed to ensure that everyone
has a decent standard of living.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:21.960
I want industry to operate in a market with
enough safeguards and infrastructure, and

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:28.129
it is not to their advantage to hurt people
in order to earn the profits that they are

00:07:28.129 --> 00:07:29.129
earning.

00:07:29.129 --> 00:07:32.479
That's why the regulation has to be strict
enough.

00:07:32.479 --> 00:07:37.310
And in some cases I actually want the government
participating in the market rather than just

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:38.310
regulating it.

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:40.099
Health care being an exception.

00:07:40.099 --> 00:07:41.099
An example of that.

00:07:41.099 --> 00:07:43.409
So this stuff is complex.

00:07:43.409 --> 00:07:48.601
The principles, people who talk about liberty
and non-aggression and they just want to talk

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.650
abstractly.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.009
They often don't want.

00:07:52.009 --> 00:07:56.699
Do or aren't able to do the difficult work
of really digging into the specifics.

00:07:56.699 --> 00:08:00.349
And you have to do it in order to really get
anywhere on this stuff.

00:08:00.349 --> 00:08:04.150
We're going to continue talking about this
